        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(channels): bundle Reef guarded claw-to-claw channel",
        "body": "Moves the Reef channel extension from openclaw/reef into the bundled extensions tree, per maintainer decision to ship it bundled rather than as an external plugin.\n\n## What\n\n- New bundled channel extension `extensions/reef` — guarded, end-to-end-encrypted claw-to-claw messaging (pairing via friend codes, dual pinned-model guards, hash-chained audit, per-friend autonomy budgets).\n- Wire protocol vendored under `extensions/reef/protocol` (self-contained; deps: noble crypto). The relay worker, protocol spec, and marketing site stay in openclaw/reef.\n- Manifest ships `channelConfigs` metadata (including host-written `enabled`) so config validation and setup surfaces work before runtime load.\n\n## Fixes folded in from first production run (validated live on a real gateway)\n\n- Monotonic device-auth timestamps: identical same-second signed requests produced identical deterministic Ed25519 signatures and collided with the relay replay key, 409ing channel start.\n- Runtime status reporting via `ctx.setStatus` + runtime-merged `buildAccountSnapshot` (was: permanent `health:not-running`).\n- Abort-aware inbox reconnect/backoff and reconcile loop (was: channel stop exceeded its 5s abort budget).\n- Per-socket settled-state gate so stale socket events cannot overwrite lifecycle state.\n- Guard admission accepts documented undated gpt-5.6 ids (sol/terra/luna) alongside dated snapshots; bare family aliases stay rejected. Owner-accepted residual risk, documented inline.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `pnpm tsgo:extensions` clean\n- `node scripts/test-projects.mjs extensions/reef` — 102 passed, 2 skipped (extension + vendored protocol suites)\n- Full changed-scope checks pass except the root `lint` shard, which fails on pre-existing `src/skills/workshop/experience-review.ts:357` from #105674 (untouched by this branch)\n- End-to-end validated against the production relay on a live gateway: pairing, guarded inbound (live gpt-5.6-terra verdicts), agent auto-reply, outbound guard, receipts\n\nFollow-up (separate PR in openclaw/reef): drop the now-duplicated extension there and point its e2e harness at this bundled copy.\n",
